#: seo-optimized-images-settings.php:173
msgid "How does it work?"
msgstr ""

#: seo-optimized-images-settings.php:177
msgid ""
"1. The plugin dynamically replaces the alt tags with the pattern specified "
"by you. It makes no changes to the database."
msgstr ""

#: seo-optimized-images-settings.php:178
msgid ""
"2. Since there are no changes to the database, one can have different alt "
"tags for same images on different pages/posts."
msgstr ""

#: seo-optimized-images-settings.php:187
msgid "Why optimize alt tags?"
msgstr ""

#: seo-optimized-images-settings.php:195
#, php-format
msgid ""
"1. According to <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"%s\">this post</a> on the Google "
"Webmaster Blog, Google tends to focus on the information in the ALT text. "
"Creating optimized alt tags can bring more traffic from Search Engines"
msgstr ""

#: seo-optimized-images-settings.php:207
msgid ""
"2. Take note that the plugin does not make changes to the database. It "
"dynamically replaces the tags at the times of page load."
msgstr ""

#: seo-optimized-images-settings.php:223
#, php-format
msgid ""
"1. For any queries contact us via the <a href='%s' target='_blank'>support "
"forums</a>."
